# Relay v0.1 OSS - CODEOWNERS
#
# Per sub-feature w12.1 (release-pypi-trusted-publish), the release
# pipeline files require Chandler (release engineering owner) review
# before merge. This file plus the GitHub `release` environment's
# required_reviewers rule together enforce VAL-W12-003 (manual
# approval before publish): the environment gate runs at deploy time;
# CODEOWNERS gates the PR-time approval that lets the workflow file
# itself change.
#
# Format: https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-security/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
#
# When sub-features w12.2..w12.6 land, they will add additional
# owners for their respective paths (TS release, SLSA workflow,
# in-toto layout, sidecar bundle, verify-install). Until then,
# Chandler is the sole owner of the release surface.

# Release pipeline: PyPI publish workflow + supporting guard scripts.
/.github/workflows/release-pypi.yml          @chandlervaughn
/.github/CODEOWNERS                          @chandlervaughn
/scripts/check-pypi-publish-workflow.py      @chandlervaughn
/scripts/check-semver-monotonic.py           @chandlervaughn
/scripts/check-pre-announcement.py           @chandlervaughn

# Release docs: runbook + announcements.
/docs/release/                               @chandlervaughn

# W17.3 conformance: contract DSL + cel-spec corpus. The nightly
# drift workflow (.github/workflows/nightly-cel-drift.yml) auto-assigns
# the GitHub issue opened on conformance drift to the first owner
# listed here (per VAL-W17-014 and C-MIN-007 alerting-path
# reconciliation).
/packages/contracts/                         @chandlervaughn
/packages/contracts-typescript/              @chandlervaughn
/tests/conformance/cel-spec/                 @chandlervaughn
/.github/workflows/nightly-cel-drift.yml     @chandlervaughn
/scripts/check-cel-spec-drift.py             @chandlervaughn
